($bc30287$love-friends-27$bc30287$,$bc30288$small_gap_both_content$bc30288$,$bc30289$Case dismissed. Signal strength, matched.$bc30289$,$bc30290$$bc30290$,$bc30291$You both go quiet in group chats at about the same rate, which means neither of you is silently more disengaged from your social circles than the other, you're running the same signal strength. That matched pattern means when one of you does go quiet, it reads as normal life happening, not a red flag either of you has to explain.$bc30291$,$bc30292$name one thing that actually causes your quiet stretches. same.$bc30292$,$bc30293$Case dismissed. Signal strength, matched.$bc30293$,$bc30294$Approved v4 template$bc30294$,$bc30295$Shared Discovery$bc30295$,$bc30296$$bc30296$,$bc30297$name one thing that actually causes your quiet stretches.$bc30297$,$bc30298$same.$bc30298$,$bc30299$Both of you describe your actual group chat habits to each other and notice how closely they match.$bc30299$,$bc30300$Case dismissed. Signal strength, matched.$bc30300$),
($bc30301$love-friends-27$bc30301$,$bc30302$small_gap_split$bc30302$,$bc30303$Case dismissed. Verdict, overturned.$bc30303$,$bc30304$[A] = the partner who indicated it bothers them.$bc30304$,$bc30305$Same amount of chat silence, but [A]'s decided theirs means something's wrong with how connected they are, while [B] never read it that way. The silence is identical, only one of you turned it into a verdict on your social health. Dropping that verdict means [A] gets to go quiet sometimes without treating it as evidence of drifting away from people.$bc30305$,$bc30306$name, out loud, that your quiet stretches don't mean disconnection. reassure once, specifically, that it doesn't read as concerning to you.$bc30306$,$bc30307$Case dismissed. Verdict, overturned.$bc30307$,$bc30308$Approved v4 template$bc30308$,$bc30309$Rename$bc30309$,$bc30310$[A] = the partner who indicated it bothers them.$bc30310$,$bc30311$name, out loud, that your quiet stretches don't mean disconnection.$bc30311$,$bc30312$reassure once, specifically, that it doesn't read as concerning to you.$bc30312$,$bc30313$Both of you name a recent quiet stretch and confirm, together, it wasn't actually a problem.$bc30313$,$bc30314$Case dismissed. Verdict, overturned.$bc30314$),
($bc30315$love-friends-27$bc30315$,$bc30316$small_gap_both_discontent$bc30316$,$bc30317$Case dismissed. Radio silence, addressed together.$bc30317$,$bc30318$$bc30318$,$bc30319$You're both going quiet in chats at a similar rate, and you're both a little guilty about it, without realizing you're managing the exact same pull toward disengaging. Comparing notes means you can actually support each other in staying a little more present, together.$bc30319$,$bc30320$name one thing that would help you stay a bit more engaged. same.$bc30320$,$bc30321$Case dismissed. Radio silence, addressed together.$bc30321$,$bc30322$Approved v4 template$bc30322$,$bc30323$Root Swap$bc30323$,$bc30324$$bc30324$,$bc30325$name one thing that would help you stay a bit more engaged.$bc30325$,$bc30326$same.$bc30326$,$bc30327$Both of you agree on one shared reminder or habit to check group chats a little more consistently.$bc30327$,$bc30328$Case dismissed. Radio silence, addressed together.$bc30328$),
($bc30329$love-friends-27$bc30329$,$bc30330$large_gap_both_content$bc30330$,$bc30331$Case dismissed. Lighthouse and flare, both valued.$bc30331$,$bc30332$[A] = ghosts more; [B] = consistently active.$bc30332$,$bc30333$[A]'s quiet stretches aren't flakiness, they're a genuine need to step back from group input sometimes, a battery-saving mode, not a disappearance. [B]'s consistent presence isn't just habit, it's [B] genuinely enjoying staying plugged in, a steady lighthouse the group can count on. Between the two of you, you've got a lighthouse and an occasional flare, and friend groups benefit from both.$bc30333$,$bc30334$send one check-in message during your next quiet stretch, just so it doesn't read as a full disappearance. notice that [A]'s quiet stretches aren't about the group, and don't take it personally.$bc30334$,$bc30335$Case dismissed. Lighthouse and flare, both valued.$bc30335$,$bc30336$Approved v4 template$bc30336$,$bc30337$Reframe$bc30337$,$bc30338$[A] = ghosts more; [B] = consistently active.$bc30338$,$bc30339$send one check-in message during your next quiet stretch, just so it doesn't read as a full disappearance.$bc30339$,$bc30340$notice that [A]'s quiet stretches aren't about the group, and don't take it personally.$bc30340$,$bc30341$Both of you agree on one simple signal [A] can send during a quiet stretch that takes thirty seconds, just to stay lightly connected.$bc30341$,$bc30342$Case dismissed. Lighthouse and flare, both valued.$bc30342$),
